      "kind": "see",
      "title": "See it",
      "text": "The fers moves one square diagonally, in any of the four directions, and takes the same way. It comes from shatranj, the old Persian chess, where it stood where the queen stands today. Thai chess (makruk) has the same piece. The marked squares are every square it can reach.",
      "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "f": "fers" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/3F4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
      "square": "d4"
    },
    {
      "kind": "try",
      "title": "Try it",
      "text": "Move the fers to the marked square. It takes two moves.",
      "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "f": "fers" }, "fen": "7k/8/8/8/3F4/8/8/K7 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
      "square": "d4",
      "targets": ["f6"]
    },
    {
      "kind": "read",
      "title": "Strategy",
      "pages": [
        {
          "text": "The fers is a weak piece, worth a little more than a pawn. It is slow, and like a bishop it stays on squares of one colour all game: this fers is on a dark square, so it can never reach a light one.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "f": "fers" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/3F4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d4", "e5"], ["d4", "c5"]]
        },
        {
          "text": "A fers is best as a guard. It protects the pieces diagonally next to it, so it makes a steady escort for a knight or a pawn moving up the board. Here it guards the knight on d5.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "f": "fers" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/3N4/2F5/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } }
        },
        {
          "text": "A fers can't run. Here the black rook attacks it, and it can only step one square away. Keep your fers near your own pieces, where it is protected, and don't send it far from home.",
          "board": { "setup": { "base": "chess", "files": 8, "ranks": 8, "pieces": { "k": "king", "p": "pawn", "n": "knight", "f": "fers" }, "fen": "4k3/8/8/8/1r1F4/8/8/4K3 w - - 0 1", "castling": false, "promotion": { "rank": "last", "pieceTypes": ["n"] } } },
          "arrows": [["d4", "e5"]]
        }
      ]
    },
